    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1140,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        1044
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 1,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "text",
          "type": "STRING",
          "widget": {
            "name": "text"
          },
          "link": null
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Image to Image · Auto Router\n\n**Geekatplay Studio** · ComfyUI-Cluster\n\nLoad a picture and say what to do with it. A local Ollama vision model studies the image, picks the model and LoRAs, and decides how strongly to change the picture.\n\n## How to use\n\n1. Start Ollama with a vision-capable model.\n2. Choose a picture in **Load input image**.\n3. Describe the change in **Ollama Vision Style Planner**.\n4. Press **Run**.\n\n## Reading the graph\n\nGroups run left to right and are numbered in the order they execute. The **Status** row at the bottom shows what the planner decided and what the loader did.\n\n## If something fails\n\n- **Model not installed**: the loader error lists the exact files and download links. Run `install.bat`.\n- **Planner says tag matching**: Ollama was not reachable or the model tag is not pulled. The workflow still runs; the summary shows the reason.\n"
      ],
      "title": "About this workflow",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -600,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        1044
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 2,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "text",
          "type": "STRING",
          "widget": {
            "name": "text"
          },
          "link": null
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Models\n\nThe planner chooses from the models **you have installed** that are listed in `model_registry.json`:\n\n| Family | Good at | VRAM |\n|---|---|---|\n| MOSS-Image | text in images, posters, layouts, all-round | 12 GB+ |\n| FLUX.3 Klein | photography, portraits, products | 12 GB+ |\n| Krea-2 Turbo | illustration, painterly, stylised | 16 GB+ |\n| Z-Image-Turbo | fast photorealism, low VRAM | 8 GB+ |\n\nVRAM figures are estimates.\n\n## Install\n\nRun `install.bat` in the ComfyUI-Cluster folder and tick the models you want. Each model's text encoder and VAE are selected with it.\n\nFLUX.3 Klein is a gated download: accept its licence on Hugging Face and set `HF_TOKEN` first.\n\n## Ollama\n\n```\nollama pull qwen3.5:9b\n```\n\n`qwen3.5:9b` reads both text and images, so it serves every planner. Any other Ollama tag works: type it into `ollama_model`.\n\n## Pin a family\n\nSet `task_hint` on the planner to `moss_image`, `flux3`, `krea2` or `z_image` to stop it choosing another family.\n\n## Denoise\n\nThe planner sets `denoise` from your request: about 0.3-0.5 for small fixes, 0.6-0.9 for a new style. To override it, disconnect `denoise` on the KSampler and type a value."
      ],
      "title": "Models and setup",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
